{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","kind":"lemma","title":"Constituent and composite Markov-trace evaluations agree exactly","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-factorization","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-markov-trace-product"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-tmli-constituent-composite-agreement"],"tags":["markov-trace","iwahori-hecke","pawlei-basis","exact-identity"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidsKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","text":"tmli-constituent-composite-agreement.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:tmli-constituent-composite-agreement\"></a><p><em>For a hadron <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{H} \\hookrightarrow V^{\\otimes N}</code> with\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = 2(j_1 + \\cdots + j_n)</code> and braid word\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}} \\in B_N</code>, suppose <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}}</code> is\ngenerator-monotone, or a cyclic rotation of a generator-monotone word\n(<a href=\"#thm:markov-trace-product\" data-at=\"mass-theory/vertex-factorisation-markov\">Markov trace product</a>). Let\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{V}_i^{\\mathrm{const}} = z\\,a_i + b_i</code>, where\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_i\\sigma_i + b_i</code> is the Hecke reduction of the letters of\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}}</code> at generator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_i</code>. Then the constituent\nproduct and the composite trace agree:</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\prod_i \\hat{V}_i^{\\mathrm{const}}\n  =\n  \\mathrm{tr}_M(\\rho(\\beta_{\\mathfrak{H}})).</code></pre>\n<p><em>Without the monotone hypothesis the two differ in general; for\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0\\sigma_1 \\in B_3</code> the difference is\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-(q^4 + q^2 + 1)/(q^2 + 1)^2</code>.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/tmli-constituent-composite-agreement.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"13.12.8","page":"b/lem-tmli-constituent-composite-agreement","qa":{"counts":{"pass":91,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.tmli_constituent_composite_agreement","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/tmli_constituent_composite_agreement.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
